          <mxGeometry x="60" y="320" width="265" height="58" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>

        <!-- ================= NOTES ================= -->
        <mxCell id="notes" value="&lt;b&gt;ACCESS NOTES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;1. Roles&lt;/b&gt; live on User.role and are one of:&lt;br&gt;student / class_teacher / admin_teacher / admin.&lt;br&gt;SchoolMembership.role is a SEPARATE per-school role.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;2. Practice pages are open.&lt;/b&gt; /melodic, /rhythm,&lt;br&gt;/harmonic, /holistic and every /exercise/&amp;lt;id&amp;gt; page&lt;br&gt;have NO @login_required. Anyone with the URL can&lt;br&gt;reach them. Only POST /submit requires a login.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;3. Home is gated, practice is not.&lt;/b&gt; &#39;/&#39; requires&lt;br&gt;login; /sandbox is the anonymous doorway to the&lt;br&gt;same home template.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;4. Results pages&lt;/b&gt; are owner-only, unless you are&lt;br&gt;a teacher of one of that student&#39;s classes, or admin.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;5. class_teacher vs admin_teacher.&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;class_teacher = assigned_teacher_id on the Class;&lt;br&gt;can view/edit a class and its overrides, but cannot&lt;br&gt;create or delete classes.&lt;br&gt;admin_teacher = teacher_id owner; can also create,&lt;br&gt;delete, set course, and assign a class_teacher.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;6. SCHOOL AUTHORITY.&lt;/b&gt; Every school-scoped route&lt;br&gt;goes through require_school_role(): a role gate alone&lt;br&gt;would let any school&#39;s admin_teacher edit every&lt;br&gt;other school&#39;s courses. Membership changes follow&lt;br&gt;&quot;strictly below your own role&quot; — so only a site admin&lt;br&gt;can seat an admin_teacher, and anyone above&lt;br&gt;student can remove those beneath them.&lt;br&gt;(BUG-003 fixed 2026-08-28.)&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;7. NAMES ARE AUTHORITATIVE.&lt;/b&gt; The red monospace&lt;br&gt;name on each box is the same string in screens.py&lt;br&gt;and in the debug panel. Renaming a box means&lt;br&gt;renaming it in screens.py in the same commit —&lt;br&gt;tests/test_screens.py enforces the pairing." style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#FFF2CC;strokeColor=#D6B656;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=10;spacingTop=6;fontSize=10;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="405" width="290" height="620" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>

